Missing Industry Labels — Investigation Summary

A total of 13 companies in the dataset had missing or unclear industry classifications. Because acquisition-focused companies can operate across different verticals, they often lack a straightforward, standardized industry label.

Given the small number of cases, I manually reviewed each company’s official website to determine whether a clear specialization or dominant industry could be identified.

Findings

Most companies operated across multiple sectors or did not communicate a specific specialization.
For these cases, assigning an industry label would be speculative and could introduce bias.

One company, Alignment Healthcare LLC, demonstrated a clear industry identity.
Based on publicly available information, this company operates in the Healthcare sector.

Decision

12 companies with ambiguous or undefined industry focus were removed from the dataset to maintain consistency and analytical accuracy.